`AbortSignal.any` is Node 20.3+. If `engines.node` in your `package.json` is 18.x, replace the combined-signal block with a manual `AbortController` that listens to both:

```ts
const controller = new AbortController();
const onAbort = () => controller.abort();
signal?.addEventListener("abort", onAbort, { once: true });
const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeoutMs);
try {
  // ...use controller.signal, then clearTimeout(timer) in a finally
} finally {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  signal?.removeEventListener("abort", onAbort);
}
```

